<title>SOUTH AFRICA: TABLE - S.AFRICA APR-JUL SPENDING UP 11.3 PCT Y/Y.</title>
<headline>TABLE - S.AFRICA APR-JUL SPENDING UP 11.3 PCT Y/Y.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-08-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Africa's Finance</p>
<p>Department said on Friday that 13.01 billion rand was requested</p>
<p>from the exchequer in July by government departments and</p>
<p>agencies, up 1.6 percent from July 1996.</p>
<p>This brought exchequer issues for the first four months of</p>
<p>the financial year (April to July) to 59.632 billion rand, the</p>
<p>department said in a statement. The total was 11.3 percent up on</p>
<p>the 53.557 billion rand issued over the same period a year ago.</p>
<p>The department added that as revenue figures for June 1997</p>
<p>had not been finalised, a detailed breakdown of revenue would</p>
<p>not be published.</p>
<p>Detailed breakdown:</p>
<p>(rand bln)		Jul '97  Jul '96  Apr/Jul '97  Apr/Jul '96</p>
<p>Exchequer issues	13.01    12.81    59.63	  53.56	</p>
<p>Total revenue	   14.40    13.92    48.17	  43.81 </p>
<p>Borrowing requirement -7.86    -1.86    10.64	  13.11 </p>
<p>Total financing	  2.16     8.14    20.66	  18.06  </p>
